# Ruleset: Apple China
#
# Expects a mainland policy, referenced with extended-matching. Must precede Platforms/Apple.list, whose apple.com suffix would otherwise take the -cn location and Maps hosts. Those hosts carry the region inside a label (gspe19-cn-ssl, gsp10-ssl-cn), which a suffix rule cannot see, so the wildcard does that work.
#
# The mainland operated estate includes iCloud on GCBD, the .cn store, and location, Maps and search endpoints for mainland clients. These endpoints can still answer through a proxy, hiding a routing mismatch.

# Apple
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,apple.com.cn
DOMAIN-WILDCARD,gsp*-cn*.ls.apple.com
DOMAIN,api.smoot.apple.cn
DOMAIN,cl2-cn.apple.com
DOMAIN,cl4-cn.apple.com
DOMAIN,gs-loc-cn.apple.com

# iCloud
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,icloud.com.cn
